Second Plaintiff and pending before the Metropolitan Magistrate [Fast Track II], Bangalore ii. C.C. 13924 of 2021, filed by First Defendant herein U/S. 200 Cr. P. C against the Plantiffs herein and Ms. Raheela Fathima W/o. Fayazuddin and D/o. Second Plaintiff pending before VI Addl. Chief Metropolitan Magistrate Bangalore;
iii. Damages Suit in O.S 141 of 2019 pending before the VIII Assistant City Civil Court, Chennai between the parties mentioned in the cause title;
And Whereas several conciliations have been attempted between the family members and friends and by the Courts but re-union could not be achieved but however, the parties hereto have decided to give quietest to all the disputes and have arrived on the following terms:
01. The First Plaintiff and the First Defendant do not want to continue their matrimonial life and hence have mutually agreed to dissolve their marriage to this effect they have entered into a Mubara'at Deed (Mutual Divorce as per Ismalic Shariat) on 17.02.2023.
